<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huronia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wendake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huronia, or Wendake, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Wendat (Huron) Confederacy between Georgian Bay and Lake Simcoe in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. In the early 17th century it held some 20,000 to 30,000 people in palisaded villages, and it was the centre of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missions. Iroquois attacks destroyed it in 1649, and its people scattered.</p></div>
